nDescription: In your message implementation guideline (MIG) for EDI type systems, you can now choose if you want to use the full or a reduced message XSD file. The message XSD file is used in the EDI flow steps. For new MIGs, the default is the full XSD file, whereas existing MIGs continue to use reduced XSD files for compatibility reasons. See Exporting Runtime Artifacts.  As Cloud Integration (standalone) customer, see Exporting Runtime Artifacts. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-04\nValid as Of: 2025-05-04\nVersion: 2503\n\n", "--- Record 231 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: New parameter: Encoded JSON Web Key Set (JWKS) Array\nDescription: We have introduced a new parameter in the custom OpenID Connect (OIDC) configuration: Encoded JWKS Array (technical name: encodedJwksArray). With the JWKS specified, the OIDC authenticator skips the request to the issuer's jwks_uri endpoint to retrieve the keys.  The parameter is designed for scenarios where the OIDC metadata discovery endpoint (./well-known/openid-configuration) is inaccessible from the public internet, such as when the OIDC provider is behind a corporate firewall.  For more information, see OpenID Connect (OIDC).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-20\nValid as Of: 2025-08-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 232 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.45.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      Logs, Metrics, and Traces: For data enrichment, now also the resource attribute k8s.cluster.uid is attached.  Furthermore, you can configure the default for existent resource attribute k8s.cluster.name (#2039).      Traces and Metrics: Update to OTel Collector 0.130.1 (#2302).      Logs: Update to Fluent Bit 4.0.5 (#2327).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-08-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 233 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Overall Improvements\nDescription: There have been several code and stability improvements.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-20\nValid as Of: 2025-08-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 234 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: About Section available for Embedded Joule\nDescription: An About section has been added to Joule, containing application and environment details, along with an option to Download Traces, facilitating better supportability of issues.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-24\nValid as Of: 2025-08-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 235 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Attachment Feature for Task Completion in Joule\nDescription: The document attachment feature allows users to upload necessary files directly within Joule while performing tasks or transactions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-24\nValid as Of: 2025-08-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 236 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhancement to Create Time Off - August 2025\nDescription: We've made an enhancement about half-day absence to the \"Create time off\" use case.  For more information, refer to Enhancement to Create Time Off - August 2025.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-19\nValid as Of: 2025-08-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 237 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases Now Supported for Finance Management Controlling in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: The following transactional Joule Use Cases are now available for Finance Management Controlling in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition:    Manage Activity Type  Manage Profit Center  Manage Statistical Key Figures and Value  Commitment by Cost Center  Manage Direct Activity Allocation  Reassign Cost and Revenue    For more information, see Finance Management Controlling.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-19\nValid as Of: 2025-08-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 238 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Processing In-House Services in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: The following use cases are now supported by Joule:  Search for in-house service objects  Display details of in-house services  Display details of in-house service objects  Perform follow-up actions for in-house service objects  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-19\nValid as Of: 2025-08-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 239 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support Extended for Subscription Order Management in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: The following transactional Joule capabilities are now supported for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition 2023 FPS01 release onwards.    Create subscription order  Search and summarize subscription contract     For more information, see Subscription Order Management. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-19\nValid as Of: 2025-08-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n---", "\nDescription: The following transactional Joule capabilities are now supported for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition 2023 FPS01 release onwards.    Create subscription order  Search and summarize subscription contract     For more information, see Subscription Order Management. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-19\nValid as Of: 2025-08-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 240 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2025.17\nDescription: New and changed features are available for data cataloging, data integration, and data modeling.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2025.17. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-19\nValid as Of: 2025-08-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 2151 ---\nComponent: Graph\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Graph Guest user role for read-only access\nDescription: You can enable users to have read-only access to Graph and the Graph Configuration API by assigning the Graph guest role to one or more users. For more information, see:    Enabling Guest Users      Define Users for Graph    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-07\nValid as Of: 2024-10-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2152 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional selected models from IBM are supported.For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-07\nValid as Of: 2024-10-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2153 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional selected models from Mistral AI are supported.For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-07\nValid as Of: 2024-10-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2154 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: For selected models, response streaming is supported in the generative AI hub orchestration service.   For more information, see Streaming.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-07\nValid as Of: 2024-10-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2155 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional selected models from IBM are supported.  For more information, see Models and Scenarios in the Generative AI Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-07\nValid as Of: 2024-10-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2156 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional selected models from Mistral AI are supported.  For more information, see Models and Scenarios in the Generative AI Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-07\nValid as Of: 2024-10-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2157 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional module added to orchestration.  The data masking module anonymizes or pseudonymizes personally identifiable information from input.   For more information, see Build Your Orchestration Workflow.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-07\nValid as Of: 2024-10-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2158 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Developer's Guide\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Change in the Structure of the SAP BTP Developer's Guide\nDescription: The new structure of the SAP BTP Developer's Guide now follows the design-led development process. It also now contains the development best practices introduced in the former Best Practices for SAP BTP guide, now renamed to SAP BTP Administrator's Guide.  See SAP BTP Developer's Guide.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-07\nValid as Of: 2024-10-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2159 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Developer's Guide\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: New Mission: Develop an Enterprise-Grade CAP Application\nDescription: You can now develop enterprise-grade CAP applications and deploy them in SAP BTP. The Develop an Enterprise-Grade CAP Application Following the SAP BTP Developer’s Guide mission includes options for tracking changes, adding audit logs, and uploading attachments.  See Mission: Develop an Enterprise-Grade CAP Application Following the SAP BTP Developer’s Guide.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-07\nValid as Of: 2024-10-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2160 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Collecting Data and Performance Metrics\nDescription: Performance and usage metrics of applications deployed on SAP BTP can be measured using the Front-End Statistical Records (FESR) tool. The results of these metrics, called performance artifacts, are collected, and transferred to SAP Cloud ALM (CALM) service that sends the data to cloud reporting.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-30\nValid as Of: 2024-10-07\nVersion: 2409B\n\n", "--- Record 211 ---\nComponent: Business Data Orchestration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of Configure Context and Configure Object ID Behavior applications\nDescription: As of the end of this year, the applications Configure Context and Configure Object ID Behavior will be deprecated. There will be no direct replacement for these applications, as they are no longer needed for the continued distribution of master data between SAP S/4 HANA and other components.  However, please note the following:   The applications will remain available for the time being, including the option to access them via SAP S/4 HANA in Business Data Orchestration.   Roles that were previously created will continue to function as before.   Newly created roles will no longer include these entries.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-21\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 212 ---\nComponent: Automation Pilot\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: AI-Assisted Dynamic Expression Generation\nDescription: The Expression Playground of SAP Automation Pilot is enhanced with generative AI capabilities that allow you to generate dynamic expressions by providing a simple prompt. To use this feature, you need to enable the Content Generation Assistant of SAP Automation Pilot.  See Dynamic Expression Playground and Generative AI in SAP Automation Pilot.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-21\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 213 ---\nComponent: Automation Pilot\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Commercial Information in the SAP Automation Pilot Guide\nDescription: You can now refer to the new “Service Plans and Metering” page in the SAP Automation Pilot documentation. It contains important commercial information, including an overview of the available service plans, and an explanation of how quotas (API calls) are calculated for core and high-level commands. This information will help you understand how the service is billed.   See Service Plans and Metering.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-21\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 214 ---\nComponent: Automation Pilot\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Function 'reduce' Now Supported in Dynamic Expressions\nDescription: The reduce function is now supported and you can use it in your dynamic expressions.  See Supported Expression Elements. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-21\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 215 ---\nComponent: Automation Pilot\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Tags for Execution Status Change Events\nDescription: The following new tags are added to the Execution Status Change event that can be matched by SAP Alert Notification service for SAP BTP:  autopi:lastReportedStatus - the execution status which was reported by the previous Execution Status Change event  autopi:executorPath - the executor path to the exact step at which the execution failed    See Execution Status Change and Enabling Automation Pilot Events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-21\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 216 ---\nComponent: Automation Pilot\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Updated Prerequisites for Cloud Connector Integration\nDescription: The prerequisite list for integrating SAP Automation Pilot with SAP Cloud Connector has been updated to include the requirement for outbound network access to the SAP Automation Pilot Connectivity Proxy endpoints. Information about the endpoints is now included in Service Availability.  See Integrating the Service with SAP Cloud Connector. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-21\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 217 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enhancements\nDescription: Improvements were made to validate addresses in Germany. The reference data now includes a finer list of house numbers.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 218 ---\nComponent: Feature Flags Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Additional properties\nDescription: You can now define special properties for a particular feature flag, according to your business scenario.  For more information, see: Concepts → Additional Properties  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-07\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 219 ---\nComponent: Feature Flags Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Flag dependencies\nDescription: In some business cases, a delivery of a feature might depend on the availability or evaluation of other feature flags in the system. You can now add such dependency flags.  For more information, see: Concepts → Dependencies  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-07\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 220 ---\nComponent: Job Scheduling Service\nEnvironment", ", a delivery of a feature might depend on the availability or evaluation of other feature flags in the system. You can now add such dependency flags.  For more information, see: Concepts → Dependencies  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-07\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 220 ---\nComponent: Job Scheduling Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Belize Themes Removed from the Dashboard UI\nDescription: The Belize themes are removed from the user interface of the Job Scheduling service dashboard.  You can choose from the following themes:    Morning Horizon (Default)      Evening Horizon      Horizon High Contrast Black      Horizon High Contrast White  If you've been using one of the Belize themes, the system automatically switches to Horizon.       Note  Belize is deprecated as of SAPUI5 1.120. SAP recommends switching to the current Horizon theme. See Deprecated Themes and Libraries.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-18\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 361 ---\nComponent: Data Attribute Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: AutoML Model Template Scenario\nDescription: The machine learning engine behind the AutoML model template scenario has been updated. It includes now important security patches that ensure the future maintenance of this scenario.  You can still use existing AutoML deployments, but AutoML models trained before August 4, 2025 can no longer be deployed. Please retrain your AutoML models to be able to deploy and use them. We apologize for the inconvenience.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-04\nValid as Of: 2025-08-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 362 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: AI Receiver Adapter Available\nDescription: AI Adapter is available now.  See: AI Receiver Adapter\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-04\nValid as Of: 2025-08-04\nVersion: 2505\n\n--- Record 363 ---\nComponent: SAP Cloud Application Event Hub\nEnvironment: Other\nTitle: Support for routing events from SAP cloud applications to their SAP Integration Suite, advanced event mesh (AEM) system\nDescription: Configure and connect SAP Integration Suite, advanced event mesh to SAP Cloud Application Event Hub to consume business events from supported SAP cloud applications. See SAP Integration Suite, Advanced Event Mesh as a Consumer.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-04\nValid as Of: 2025-08-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 364 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Grounding Capability - Pipeline Processing Statuses for Documents\nDescription: Additional attributes are now available to identify details and pipeline processing statuses for documents in the response of the following Pipeline API endpoints of the document grounding capability:    GET <url>/pipeline/api/v1/pipeline/{pipelineId}/executions/{executionId}/documents      GET <url>/pipeline/api/v1/pipeline/{pipelineId}/executions/{executionId}/documents/{documentId}      GET <url>/pipeline/api/v1/pipeline/{pipelineId}/documents      GET <url>/pipeline/api/v1/pipeline/{pipelineId}/documents/{documentId}      The following endpoints include now pagination support:    GET <url>/pipeline/api/v1/pipeline/{pipelineId}/executions/{executionId}/documents      GET <url>/pipeline/api/v1/pipeline/{pipelineId}/documents      See Get Pipeline Status.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-01\nValid as Of: 2025-08-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 365 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Process and Workflow Instances\nDescription: The following enhancements have been made:  You can now use the Copy button to copy the entire context to your clipboard.  You can now view the Context larger than 100 KB.  See Process and Workflow Instances.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-01\nValid as Of: 2025-08-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 366 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Off-Cycle Upgrade\nDescr